%N A401291 Maximum possible smallest part in a partition of n into 3-smooth numbers, no part dividing another.
%C A401291 The question of Erdős and Lewin in the remarks on Erdős Problem 1110 is equivalent to asking whether a(n) -> infinity. The lower bounds stated there give an affirmative answer.
%H A401291 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A401291/b401291.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401291 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/1110">Erdős Problem 1110</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A401291 a(n) = n if and only if n is 3-smooth (A003586).
%Y A401291 Cf. A003586, A355915.
